From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MYIR Tech Limited <support@myirtech.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: dcmipp: select a raw sensor format for ISP paths

The DCMIPP main and auxiliary paths use the ISP and therefore require a
raw Bayer input. Sensors such as OV5640 expose processed RGB and YUV media
bus formats in addition to raw formats. Passing all of those formats to
CameraSensor::getFormat() can select RGB565, which the DCMIPP ISP input pad
rejects with EINVAL.

Restrict automatic sensor format selection to raw formats. Explicit raw
capture requests continue to select their requested media bus code.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MYIR board support]
Signed-off-by: MYIR Tech Limited <support@myirtech.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/dcmipp/dcmipp.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/dcmipp/dcmipp.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/dcmipp/dcmipp.cpp
index 5e57fd80..24bbfd1d 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/dcmipp/dcmipp.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/dcmipp/dcmipp.cpp
@@ -382,6 +382,10 @@ std::vector<uint32_t> DcmippCameraConfiguration::extractUniqueMediaBusCodes(cons
 {
 	std::set<uint32_t> uniqueCodes;
 	for (const auto &entry : inputFmt) {
+		if (PixelFormatInfo::info(entry.first).colourEncoding !=
+		    PixelFormatInfo::ColourEncodingRAW)
+			continue;
+
 		uniqueCodes.insert(entry.second);
 	}
 
